  "proved": [
    "Regularly resolving all but a leaf arc gives a connected parametrizing disk. Cutting its two copies of that arc gives exactly three embedded disks E,E\u2032,K.",
    "The irregular last switch joins E,E\u2032 into W, an embedded disk. W must have inessential boundary, or strict irregular improvement contradicts least weight.",
    "The two complementary boundary paths of W are homotopic relative endpoints. Consequently the embedded disks K+2E and K+2E\u2032 both have boundary homotopic to the essential boundary of F.",
    "Their original-edge vectors sum to 2N(F). Componentwise nonincreasing normal replacement and least weight force equality and no loss at any edge. Two-array edge rigidity and lex minimality force both normal vectors equal v(F), so N(E)=N(E\u2032) on every original edge."
  ],
  "not_proved": [
    "The two caps are normally isotopic or bound a cancellable product region.",
    "A finite simultaneous leaf/opposite-cap cancellation or the full fundamental-disk existence theorem.",
    "The general primitive extreme-ray/vertex disk theorem."
  ],
